---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Kiah Harpool — a Chicago media leader, systems thinker, and product builder working across media investment, AI workflows, products, and culture."
>
  <section class="kh-about-hero section">
    <div class="kh-about-meta">
      <span>ABOUT / KIAH HARPOOL</span>
      <span>CHICAGO, IL</span>
    </div>

    <h1>
      <span>Media person.</span>
      <span>Systems thinker.</span>
      <span>Compulsive builder.</span>
    </h1>

    <div class="kh-about-intro-grid">
      <p class="kh-about-deck">
        I’m most interested in the moment when something technically works — but could work much
        better.
      </p>
      <p class="kh-about-intro-copy">
        My work sits between media, operations, technology, and product. I like finding the hidden
        logic inside complicated work, making it clearer, and then building the thing that helps
        people move through it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="kh-about-story section" aria-labelledby="about-story">
    <div class="kh-about-section-label">
      <p class="kh-kicker">01 / THE THREAD</p>
      <h2 id="about-story">Media led me to systems. Systems led me to building.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="kh-about-story-copy">
      <p>
        I work in media investment at <strong>Publicis Media / PMX</strong>, where I lead people and
        help turn a lot of moving pieces — audiences, markets, investment decisions, process, and
        execution — into work that feels understandable and manageable.
      </p>
      <p>
        Over time, I became just as interested in <em>how</em> the work happens as the work itself.
        Where does a decision stall? What gets repeated manually? What knowledge lives in one
        person’s head? What would make the right next step obvious to someone else?
      </p>
      <p>
        That naturally pulled me toward AI and workflow design. I map decision logic, prototype
        tools, and think about adoption as part of the system — not as an afterthought. The goal is
        rarely “use AI.” The goal is usually to make complicated work clearer, faster, or easier to
        trust.
      </p>
      <p>
        The same instinct follows me outside my day job. If I keep wishing a product existed, I tend
        to build it: <strong>Duel Cut</strong> for ranking movies through head-to-head choices,
        <strong>Encore</strong> for figuring out which concerts really were the best,
        <strong>Duel Draw</strong> for playing a drawing game directly with one other person, and
        <strong>Points</strong> for exploring a more focused, ritual-driven guided practice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="kh-about-ledger section" aria-labelledby="about-now">
    <div class="kh-about-section-label">
      <p class="kh-kicker">02 / CURRENTLY</p>
      <h2 id="about-now">A few useful coordinates.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="kh-about-facts">
      <article>
        <span class="kh-about-fact-number">01</span>
        <div>
          <span class="kh-about-fact-label">WORK</span>
          <h3>Media investment + team leadership</h3>
          <p>Publicis Media / PMX, with a focus on strategy, execution, people, and better systems.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span class="kh-about-fact-number">02</span>
        <div>
          <span class="kh-about-fact-label">SYSTEMS</span>
          <h3>AI workflows + decision logic</h3>
          <p>Finding repeatable friction and turning it into workflows, tools, and clearer choices.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span class="kh-about-fact-number">03</span>
        <div>
          <span class="kh-about-fact-label">BUILDING</span>
          <h3>Duel Cut / Encore / Duel Draw / Points</h3>
          <p>Independent products built because the version I wanted to use did not exist yet.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span class="kh-about-fact-number">04</span>
        <div>
          <span class="kh-about-fact-label">COMMUNITY</span>
          <h3>Media Advertising Club of Chicago</h3>
          <p>Industry programming, leadership, mentorship, and giving people a reason to show up.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="kh-about-method section" aria-labelledby="about-method">
    <div class="kh-about-section-label">
      <p class="kh-kicker">03 / HOW I WORK</p>
      <h2 id="about-method">The method is usually the same.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="kh-about-principles">
      <article>
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>Find the friction.</h3>
        <p>The workaround, repeated question, confusing handoff, or tiny annoyance is usually the clue.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>Map the logic.</h3>
        <p>Before automating anything, I want to know what decision is actually being made and why.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>Make it tangible.</h3>
        <p>A prototype answers questions that another meeting, deck, or abstract discussion cannot.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>04</span>
        <h3>Make it usable by someone else.</h3>
        <p>A clever system is not finished until another person can understand it, trust it, and use it.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="kh-about-interests section" aria-labelledby="about-interests">
    <div>
      <p class="kh-kicker">04 / OFF THE CLOCK</p>
      <h2 id="about-interests">Culture is part of the operating system.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="kh-about-interests-copy">
      <p>
        I’m a music person, a movie person, and the kind of person who will turn either one into a
        ranking system if given enough time. I care about concerts, records, film, books, design,
        Chicago, and the strange little artifacts that make culture feel specific instead of generic.
      </p>
      <p>
        Those interests are not separate from how I work. They are usually where the product ideas
        start — with curiosity, taste, and a question I cannot stop trying to answer.
      </p>
      <a class="kh-pill" href={withBase('/works/')}>See what I’m building →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .kh-about-hero,
  .kh-about-story,
  .kh-about-ledger,
  .kh-about-method,
  .kh-about-interests {
    color: #5A1F4F;
  }

  .kh-about-meta {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .kh-about-hero h1 {
    max-width: 15ch;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(4.5rem, 10.8vw, 11rem);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: -0.065em;
    line-height: 0.78;
  }

  .kh-about-hero h1 span {
    display: block;
  }

  .kh-about-hero h1 span:nth-child(2) {
    margin-left: clamp(0rem, 6vw, 7rem);
  }

  .kh-about-intro-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.85fr) minmax(18rem, 0.6fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 8vw, 9rem);
    align-items: start;
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem);
  }

  .kh-about-deck {
    max-width: 25ch;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 4.25rem);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    line-height: 0.98;
  }

  .kh-about-intro-copy {
    max-width: 35rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.5vw, 1.3rem);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .kh-about-story,
  .kh-about-ledger,
  .kh-about-method,
  .kh-about-interests {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(14rem, 0.42fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 9rem);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(90, 31, 79, 0.25);
  }

  .kh-about-section-label h2,
  .kh-about-interests h2 {
    max-width: 12ch;
    margin: 0.85rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 5vw, 5.5rem);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
    line-height: 0.9;
  }

  .kh-about-story-copy {
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .kh-about-story-copy p {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 1.5vw, 1.32rem);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .kh-about-story-copy p:first-child {
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.2vw, 1.9rem);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .kh-about-facts {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(90, 31, 79, 0.2);
  }

  .kh-about-facts article {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding: 1.8rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(90, 31, 79, 0.2);
  }

  .kh-about-fact-number,
  .kh-about-fact-label,
  .kh-about-principles article > span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.075em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .kh-about-fact-number {
    opacity: 0.55;
  }

  .kh-about-fact-label {
    color: #A23D3D;
  }

  .kh-about-facts h3 {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 3.2rem);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 0.98;
  }

  .kh-about-facts p {
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 0.7rem 0 0;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .kh-about-principles {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .kh-about-principles article {
    min-height: 15rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1.5px solid #5A1F4F;
    border-radius: 22px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .kh-about-principles article:nth-child(1),
  .kh-about-principles article:nth-child(4) {
    background: #D7CAF5;
  }

  .kh-about-principles article:nth-child(2) {
    background: #F7E8EA;
  }

  .kh-about-principles article:nth-child(3) {
    background: #B39FEF;
  }

  .kh-about-principles h3 {
    margin: auto 0 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 3.6rem);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    line-height: 0.92;
  }

  .kh-about-principles p {
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .kh-about-interests-copy {
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .kh-about-interests-copy p {
    margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.4vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .kh-about-interests-copy .kh-pill {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .kh-about-meta {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.35rem;
      margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }

    .kh-about-hero h1 {
      font-size: clamp(3.7rem, 17vw, 6rem);
      line-height: 0.82;
    }

    .kh-about-hero h1 span:nth-child(2) {
      margin-left: 0;
    }

    .kh-about-intro-grid,
    .kh-about-story,
    .kh-about-ledger,
    .kh-about-method,
    .kh-about-interests {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }

    .kh-about-intro-grid {
      margin-top: 3rem;
    }

    .kh-about-section-label h2,
    .kh-about-interests h2 {
      font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 13vw, 4.8rem);
    }

    .kh-about-principles {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .kh-about-principles article {
      min-height: 12rem;
    }
  }
</style>
